body:
`name` gives a store path and `nix profile list` entry with no version. Deriving it from the same `pub const version` line that `release.yml` greps keeps it correct without anyone having to remember this file at release time.

```suggestion
            pname = "fx";
            version =
              let
                line = pkgs.lib.findFirst (pkgs.lib.hasPrefix "pub const version = ") null
                  (pkgs.lib.splitString "\n" (builtins.readFile ./src/main.zig));
              in
              pkgs.lib.removeSuffix "\";" (pkgs.lib.removePrefix "pub const version = \"" line);
```

`./.` copies the whole tree, so `tests/`, `sdk/` and `.github/` land in the store and any docs-only commit invalidates the build. Mirroring `.paths` from `build.zig.zon` takes the source closure from 30.5 MiB to 25.5 MiB here.

```suggestion
            src = pkgs.lib.fileset.toSource {
              root = ./.;
              fileset = pkgs.lib.fileset.unions [
                ./build.zig
                ./build.zig.zon
                ./src
                ./LICENSE
                ./THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
              ];
            };
```

`pkgs.zig` and `pkgs.zig_0_16` are the same derivation on your pin today, but `zig` follows nixpkgs, so the next lock bump moves it off the `minimum_zig_version` in `build.zig.zon`. `versionCheckHook` also makes the build fail if the installed binary stops reporting the version parsed above.

```suggestion
            nativeBuildInputs = [ pkgs.makeBinaryWrapper pkgs.zig_0_16 ];
            doInstallCheck = true;
            nativeInstallCheckInputs = [ pkgs.versionCheckHook ];
            versionCheckProgramArg = "--version";
```

`description` and `homepage` show up in `nix search`, and `platforms` keeps the package from evaluating on systems fx does not ship.

```suggestion
            meta = {
              description = "Tiny, open, embeddable, native coding agent";
              homepage = "https://fx.sh";
              license = pkgs.lib.licenses.asl20;
              mainProgram = "fx";
              platforms = [ "aarch64-darwin" "aarch64-linux" "x86_64-darwin" "x86_64-linux" ];
            };
```
